       "desc": "Straight CF reducer that joins two different flange sizes in line, with a rotatable reduced-size flange; 304 or 316L stainless steel.",
       "about": [
        "Use it to step a CF line down, or up, between two nominal sizes, for example from a DN100 chamber port to a DN40 pump line. The smaller flange is rotatable for bolt alignment.",
        "Main flange sizes are DN40, DN63, DN100 and DN160, with reducer flanges of DN16, DN40, DN63 and DN100. The DN40/16, DN63/16, DN63/40, DN100/40, DN100/63 and DN160/40 versions are 70 mm long; DN160/63 and DN160/100 are 127 mm. Stainless Steel 304 / 1.4301 or 316L / 1.4404 is used for tube and flanges. Pressure range is 1 × 10⁻¹² mbar to ambient, tightness ≤ 1 × 10⁻¹⁰ mbar l/s, bake-out up to 450 °C.",
        "Tubes are glass bead blasted; polished finish is available on request. Other nominal diameters and dimensions can also be quoted. Contact Vacprotech for pricing and availability."
       ],
